The env_0051_self_storage_operator scenario is delivered. Both tasks in each of the 5 difficulties pass the policy audit and the document audit, every gate is green, and `validate_scenario` prints VALID.

The company is Bluegate Self Storage, with 7 products. The 5 difficulties (2 tasks each) are:

| Difficulty | Product | Documents | Audit rounds (policy / documents) |
|---|---|---|---|
| storage_unit_account_servicing | unit | 69 | 3 / 3 |
| parking_rate_increase_and_compliance | parking | 66 | 4 / 2 |
| tenant_protection_claims | protect | 68 | 5 / 2 |
| moving_truck_rentals | truck | 64 | 4 / 2 |
| autopay_authorization_changes | autopay | 51 | 4 / 2 |

The two products no difficulty uses, prepaid rent plans (17 documents) and business accounts (19 documents), passed their render gates only. As the pipeline allows, they were never audited.

How the run went:
- **Account cuts:** the usage limit cut off agents three times. Each time I checked what was actually on disk and resumed the same agent, so no work was redone.
- **Pipelining:** agent calls in one batch only return together, so I ran the steps batch by batch rather than truly pipelined. To keep work moving I started rendering documents before the last difficulty passed its policy audit. I chose only renders whose inputs that audit couldn't change.
- **Policy audits:** the reworks mostly fixed factor tiers no customer could reach, overrides of base rules that weren't declared, an unrealistic truck pricing rule, and stale figures left in task design notes.
- **Document audits:** some documents had wording slips. The auditors also found contradictions in the source files themselves, such as a tool description disagreeing with its policy. I sent those back through task rework and policy re-audit, then re-rendered and re-audited the documents. Only one scored value changed: truck task 0's additional-day charge went from 14.83 to 22.24, because the old value landed exactly on a half-cent and the rule gives no tie-breaking rounding.
- **Base-text slip:** I didn't tell the protection renderer up front that frozen base text must render as written, and it rewrote one base description. I had it restored before the document re-audit.

There are four known issues in the frozen base charter. Base can't be edited after fan-out, so each was either worked around in that difficulty's own policies or left as is. None changes a scored value, and all are logged as `BLUEPRINT-KNOWN` in the worklog:
- The facility lookup tool can only find a unit or space by an inventory id no caller has, so no task includes a unit transfer.
- Two parking checks require the caller to state an internal agreement id; parking replaced them with its own declared rules.
- In protection claims, the reconsideration and free-look time limits apply where they can never hold; protection retired both with declared overrides.
- Two descriptions of base figures still read as if a retired clause were in force: the protection annual limit and the AutoPay draft amount setting.

Everything is in `env/env_0051_self_storage_operator/`. `worklog.md` has the full run history, `audits/` has every audit report, and `.audit_views/` holds the masked views the reports cite by hash. My scratch scripts are in `/tmp/run_0051/`.
